1. **A data processing system comprising:**

a host comprising a memory storing a receive queue assigned to a software process executing on the host;

a network interface controller coupled to the host; and

an accelerator module disposed in a data path between a packet network and the network interface controller, the accelerator module being configured to:

receive, from the packet network, packets of a packet stream associated with the software process;

process the packet stream on behalf of the software process to generate a processing result;

encapsulate the processing result in one or more result packets comprising information identifying the receive queue; and

cause the one or more result packets to be written, through the network interface controller, to the receive queue in the memory of the host.

1. **A data processing system comprising:**

a host processor configured to execute host software;

a memory coupled to the host processor;

a network interface controller comprising at least one receive queue accessible by the host software through a receive-queue interface;

packet-processing hardware coupled to the network interface controller and configured to:

receive a network packet before the network packet is delivered to the host software;

perform, independently of the host processor, at least one packet-processing operation on the network packet to produce a processed packet; and

cause the processed packet to be placed in a host-memory receive buffer associated with the at least one receive queue and cause receive-queue state of the network interface controller to identify the host-memory receive buffer as containing a received packet,

wherein the network interface controller is configured, based on the receive-queue state, to notify the host software of availability of the processed packet through the receive-queue interface, such that the processed packet is delivered to the host software via a normal receive-queue mechanism of the network interface controller without requiring the host software to use an offload-specific packet-delivery interface.
